          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Thunderwolf Cavalry" id="0484-dc86-ec02-a7f0" hidden="false">
              <description>All close combat attacks made by a model with a Thunderwolf mount have the Rending (6+) special rule. In addition, a model upgraded to have a Thunderwolf mount increases their Strength, Attacks and Wounds characteristics by 1 and gains the Hammer of Wrath (1), Relentless, Hit and Run and Cavalry special rules (these bonuses are already included in the profiles of models that have a Thunderwolf mount as part of their standard wargear).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Formations" id="9762-4621-c983-5eb5" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="1868-1270-2edb-69e0" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
      </costs>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Pride of the Legion" id="dfdd-30fa-8eb9-c56b" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="724a-d77b-6a61-4bd0" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Pride of the Legion" id="8435-364b-6dab-e3f8" hidden="false">
              <description>In the gravest wars, the Lion entrusts each Legion’s Praetorian to gather the finest of their warriors for the spearhead. In such hosts, only Veterans and Terminators form the battleline.

•Legion Veteran squads and Terminator squads are Troops choices in the Force, and units of either of these types must be selected as the Force’s Compulsory Troops choices. This also includes any Legion specific Terminator squads which are also Elites choices.
• Command squads may take a Land Raider of either the Proteus or Phobos type as a Dedicated Transport.

Limitations
• Should all Legion Veteran Tactical squads and Terminator squads in the Force be destroyed in the battle, then the enemy counts as having scored an additional Secondary Objective worth 2 Victory points.
• You may not take an Allied Force Detachment.
• The majority of the units in the detachment must have the Legiones Astartes special rule (so if the detachment comprises seven units, at least four must have the Legiones Astartes rule, for example)
• An army using this Formation may not include more non-Infantry units than it does Infantry units.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
