    <selectionEntryGroup name="Space Wolf Warlord Traits" id="4931-5179-77e7-06cf" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="d3ba-b0f5-de47-3d85" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Howl of the Death Wolf" id="8359-b34c-ab94-f7c1" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="15d2-73b7-3e4f-dcdf" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Fleet" id="493b-86ca-8845-9a83" hidden="false" targetId="b1ba-0709-4305-88e2" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="name" type="set" value="Howl of the Wolf"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
          </infoLinks>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Howl of the Wolf" id="96bd-2c79-da65-fcd8" hidden="false">
              <description>With a single howl from the Warlords lips, the Rout is spurred to action, taking the final killing sprint to deliver the death blow all to the echoing cry of his warriors. Once per game, a Warlord with this trait may declare it will howl. For the rest of that turn, all Space Wolves units in your army gain the benefits of the Fleet (2) special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Resolve of the Bear" id="bfb5-0e15-56dd-674d" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="3c97-e0b9-13ae-6d2d" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Feel No Pain" id="9222-1077-3b64-b35a" hidden="false" targetId="f3a2-c2b0-6b0e-1653" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="name" type="set" value="Feel no Pain (5)"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
          </infoLinks>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="3c97-e0b9-13ae-6d2d" type="set" value="0">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="6896-87ba-b73a-29d4" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Resolve of the Bear" id="af5a-8417-de3f-c819" hidden="false">
              <description>The Warlord is as strong and as stable as any mountain, drawing upon their totem of the unyielding and stoic bear. The Warlord gains the Feel no Pain (5+) special rule. In addition, all attacks against a model with this Warlord trait have -1 to all wounds rolls.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Rage of the Berserker" id="18df-4b59-2740-cf31" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="eb36-9127-f728-38e0" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Rage" id="bf55-9e0e-65c9-a1de" hidden="false" targetId="8c0c-8856-f1ab-923d" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="name" type="set" value="Rage (3)"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
          </infoLinks>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Rage of the Berserker" id="9118-ca4e-9957-e37b" hidden="false">
              <description>The Warlord channels the fury of a Berserker like few others. Many of his men speak that he is already taken with the curse of the Wulfen. This Warlord gains the Rage (3) special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Space Wolves Formations" id="2078-7859-4d99-afc6" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="5551-f5cf-a68e-edf4" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="The Emperor&apos;s Executioners" id="9748-aba8-efca-d4c3" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="471e-accd-0242-48e8" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Fearless" id="5769-1b7a-e80b-7a1a" hidden="false" targetId="8220-efb5-2199-6d3d" type="rule"/>
            <infoLink name="Hatred" id="a80b-8030-616b-3366" hidden="false" targetId="a6b0-c95c-c78f-b0ab" type="rule"/>
            <infoLink name="Preferred Enemy" id="8ba2-2489-77b0-5c8c" hidden="false" targetId="5ebf-6f3b-e001-fd3e" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Emperor&apos;s Executioners" id="8d87-2ab9-b184-a581" hidden="false" publicationId="cfcf-7aa1-fe59-68ec">
              <description>As the Emperor&apos;s Executioners, the Space Wolves were tasked with a singular purpose – to hunt down and eradicate the enemies of the Imperium without mercy or remorse. The foes of mankind trembled at the mention of the Space Wolves, for they were a Legion that specialized in bringing swift and brutal justice to those who dared defy the Imperium. In the crucible of  civil war, the Space Wolves prove once again that they were the Emperor&apos;s Executioners, his chosen warriors to mete out his judgment upon those who dared betray the Imperium

Effects
• All models with the Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves) special rule in a Detachment using this Rite of War gain the Hatred (Chaos Space Marines) Hatred (Primaris Space Marines) and Preferred Enemy (Primarch) special rules.
• All models in a Detachment using this Rite of War gain the Fearless special rule when locked in combat with a Primarch that has the Demon special rule.
• When a unit from a Detachment using this Formation has a Charge declared for it targeting an enemy unit that includes a model with the Primarch Unit Type, that unit gains a bonus of +2 to its Charge roll made to determine its Charge Distance.
Limitations
• This Formation may only be taken by an Allied Detachment with the Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves) Faction, and may never be taken for a Primary Detachment
• A Detachment with this Formation may not include any models with the Vehicle or Primarch Unit Type.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="The Bloodied Claw" id="3638-c6df-a92f-31ef" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="2035-77fd-e4cd-0209" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Fleet" id="8845-c0ef-24d9-d97a" hidden="false" targetId="b1ba-0709-4305-88e2" type="rule"/>
            <infoLink name="Furious Charge" id="d876-e50c-d9a4-e11f" hidden="false" targetId="7ddc-eea7-3935-d6d4" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Bloodied Claw" id="836b-58f1-86b8-2e30" hidden="false" page="199" publicationId="cfcf-7aa1-fe59-68ec">
              <description>A dire ritual of the Space Wolves unfolds when the sons of Fenris are set loose upon the battlefield. In the frenzied wake of this invocation, the warriors gain enhanced prowess, embodying the relentless pursuit and devastating charges emblematic of their savage nature. 

Effects
• Once per battle, at the start of their player turn, a player whose army includes a Detachment using this Formation may declare a Bloody Claw. Once the Bloody Claw is declared and until the start of the controlling player’s next turn, all models with the Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves) special rule in the Detachment with this Formation gain the following benefits:
- Add +1 to the score used to determine the winner of any Assault (this is not cumulative, and no individual combat may have it applied more than once).
- Gain the Fleet (3) and Furious Charge (1) special rules. 
Limitations
• During the turn in which the controlling player has declared the Bloody Claw, all units that include one or more models with the Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves) special rule in this Detachment capable of Charging must always attempt to Charge an enemy unit in the Assault phase if there are any eligible targets in range and line of sight. If multiple eligible targets are available, the controlling player may choose which to declare a Charge against.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Wolfclaw Strike Force" id="b2d5-0b91-3627-606d" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Fear" id="0c47-738e-2563-c6d3" hidden="false" targetId="bbca-34a4-2d3d-8d2a" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Wolf Claw Strike Force" id="7830-f2c4-76fe-7aac" hidden="false">
              <description>The Wolfclaw Strike Force, a fearsome arm of the Space Wolves&apos; martial might, is a specialized formation meticulously crafted for surgical strikes and lightning-fast assaults. Comprising elite packs of Swiftclaw bikers, Blood Claws, and the legendary Thunderwolf Cavalry, the strike force epitomizes the Fenrisian wolves&apos; predatory swiftness on the battlefield. With a seamless coordination of mounted and infantry elements, the Wolfclaw Strike Force prowls the war-torn realms, delivering swift, devastating blows and embodying the relentless hunting instincts of the Space Wolves.

Effects
• Counter-charge: At the end of your opponent’s Charge sub-phase, you can declare a charge with one unengaged unit from this Detachment, so long as the enemy unit that you attempt to charge is has itself completed a charge on this turn. Any units that do so count as charging for all rules purposes.
• The Howl of Wolves: As long as the Wolf Claw Strike Force&apos;s Warlord is still alive, all units in that model’s formation have the Fear (1) special rule.

Limitations
• This formation must include at least one of the following: A Wolf Lord or the Primarch Leman Russ. 
• This formation must include at least one Stormwolf Gunship and as least two units of Thunderwolf Cavalary.
• Grey Hunter Packs must be taken as compulsory troops choices in this formation.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Blood Angels Formations" id="562e-d631-5b5d-ac26" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="The Day of Revelation" id="9aa2-ef71-713f-2f4a" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="cc49-396c-d53d-37d8" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Day of Revelation" id="7007-a3f2-1b41-b42c" hidden="false">
              <description>Based upon a campaign of “open domination”, during the Horus Heresy, Sanguinius himself would lead a host of crimson Angels from the heavens above, conquering a world with fire and flame. In more modern times, this formation has been adapted by the Blood Angels in it&apos;s own way. 

Effects
• At the start of the battle, before any models are deployed or which player will take the first turn is decided, the controlling player of a Detachment using this Rite of War must declare to their opponent a Turn number from Turn 2 - 4, indicating on which of their own turns they will bring their Deep Strike Assault into play. Then the controlling player places a marker anywhere on the battlefield, indicating the point where the first unit of the Deep Strike Assault will be placed.
• A Deep Strike Assault which includes only units from a Detachment using this Rite of War does not make Reserves rolls to see when it may enter play – instead the controlling player must bring the Deep Strike Assault into play at the start of the Turn chosen at the start of the battle. In addition, the first model placed to determine where the Deep Strike arrives must be placed within 6&quot; of the marker placed at the start of the battle, and does not scatter (if the first model cannot be placed at least 1&quot; away from an enemy model because of these restrictions then the controlling player may choose to place it anywhere on the battlefield, but must then scatter the model after placing it).
• All units from a Detachment using this Rite of War that are deployed onto the battlefield normally and are not placed into Reserves gain the Fearless special rule until the start of the controlling player’s second turn.

Limitations
• Compulsory HQ choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War must be made up entirely of models with Jump-Packs.
• All units that are made up entirely of models with the Deep Strike special rule in a Detachment using this Rite of War must be assigned to a Deep Strike Assault.
• A Detachment using this Rite of War may not take any Fortification choices or any model with a Movement Characteristic of 0 or ‘-’, or that is otherwise unable to move, unless that model also has the Orbital Assault Vehicle special rule.
• A Detachment using this Rite of War may not include any models with the Subterranean Assault special rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Blood Angels Wargear" id="982b-928a-c4fd-ac78" collective="false" hidden="true" import="true">
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="9080-889f-6881-4abf" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="roster" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Gleaming Pinions" id="970b-0731-6539-b958" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="1e25-291d-00e4-9e0c" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="5"/>
          </costs>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink name="Hammer of Wrath" id="7a79-fbaa-e0e0-349d" hidden="false" targetId="a4d3-4e19-13d9-508e" type="rule">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier field="name" type="set" value="Hammer of Wrath (1)"/>
              </modifiers>
            </infoLink>
          </infoLinks>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Gleaming Pinions" id="2c62-4fdd-ba1b-824e" hidden="false" typeId="d4b8-6c36-8bad-c884" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="a1cc-ea5e-6a1d-d78e">A model with Gleaming Pinions gains the Hammer of Wrath (1) special rule. In addition, this model may re-roll charges in the charge phase.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Blood Angels Warlord Traits" id="f40d-eab1-ea10-1ee9" collective="false" hidden="true" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="a3ac-5dd8-541c-c79a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
          <conditions>
            <condition childId="9080-889f-6881-4abf" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="roster" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="The Gift of Foresight" id="9700-f6cf-8de1-e726" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="4989-a01b-d8cb-b33e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Gift of Foresight" id="7425-1cb4-bf1f-ddf5" hidden="false">
              <description>This heroic warrior bears a glimmering of Sanguinius’ prophetic gifts. Flashes of foresight allow him to parry and weave around his enemy’s blows with supernatural speed and skill.
This warlord gains the Preternatural Skill and Precision Strikes special rules.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Encarmine Paladin" id="b48c-f29d-1691-594a" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="8998-e146-3587-7bee" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="2753-3fda-80c3-0d79" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Encarmine Paladin" id="0931-ca60-afb2-9ce9" hidden="false">
              <description>A Warlord with this Trait gains the Fear (1) special rule when the enemy army has the Chaos Space Marine special rule. Whenever a Warlord with this Trait is on the winning side of a combat in which the Warlord was Engaged and that includes at least one enemy model with the Chaos Space Marine rule, he increases the value of his Fear special rule by one point at the end of the Assault phase in which the combat is won, to a maximum of Fear (4).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Paragon of Unity" id="f7af-8a76-7167-18ee" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="f5e4-9e92-3300-8e70" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
            <constraint id="e45d-e44b-b555-658b" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Paragon of Unity" id="8701-be20-ff12-c8bc" hidden="false">
              <description>This hero inspires all on the battlefield to fight to their best. Once per game, this Warlord may raise his voice to inspire his troops. Any friendly unit made up entirely of models with the Legiones Astartes (Blood Angels) special rule that can draw a line of sight to the Warlord gains a bonus of +1 to their Leadership  and Weapon Skill Characteristics, to a maximum of 10.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
